IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `acc-types`

-- Accident Compensation Act 2001 — GOAL 1: DOES THE PERSON HAVE COVER, AND
-- WHAT KIND OF INJURY IS IT?
--
--   "Was there an accident and a personal injury; does the person have cover
--    under s 20, 21, 21B or 22; is the injury a treatment injury,
--    work-related, a motor vehicle injury or a non-work injury; and which
--    Account pays?"
--
-- Source: ../source/ACC2001.txt — Part 1 (ss 6, 16-18A) and Part 2
-- (ss 20-38), Schedules 2, 3, 3A; ss 166, 167, 213, 218, 227, 228.

§ `Goal 1 — cover and classification`

§§ `Accident and personal injury (ss 25-27)`

-- s 25(1): (a) a specific event involving an external force, a sudden
-- movement to avoid one, or a twist; (b) inhaling on a specific occasion,
-- "which ... does not include the inhalation of a virus, bacterium,
-- protozoan, or fungus, unless that inhalation is the result of the criminal
-- act of a person other than the injured person"; (ba) ingestion likewise
-- (fungus allowed); (c) a burn or radiation, not "caused by exposure to the
-- elements"; (d) absorbing a chemical "within a defined period of time not
-- exceeding 1 month"; (e) exposure to the elements within a month that "for
-- a continuous period exceeding 1 month" restricts the person, or causes
-- death; (f) a Schedule 3A birth injury. FORK F1: "1 month" is read as
-- 30 days and "exceeding 1 month" as more than 30 days.
@ref s 25(1)
GIVEN o IS AN Occurrence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occurrence is an accident` o IF
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `(a) a specific event with an external force, a sudden avoiding movement, or a twist` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `(b) inhaling something on a specific occasion` microbe criminal THEN (NOT microbe) OR criminal
    WHEN `(ba) orally ingesting something on a specific occasion` microbe criminal THEN (NOT microbe) OR criminal
    WHEN `(c) a burn or exposure to radiation on a specific occasion` elements THEN NOT elements
    WHEN `(d) absorbing a chemical through the skin` days THEN days AT MOST 30
    WHEN `(e) exposure to the elements or extremes of temperature` days restricted dies THEN
        days AT MOST 30 AND (restricted GREATER THAN 30 OR dies)
    WHEN `(f) an internal force during labour causing a Schedule 3A birth injury` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 25(2)(a), (2A): treatment by a registered health professional (or an
-- overseas equivalent) is not an accident — except a birth injury under (1)(f).
@ref s 25(2)-(2A)
GIVEN o IS AN Occurrence, `the occurrence is treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an accident under s 25, occurrence` o `, treatment:` `the occurrence is treatment` IF
    `the occurrence is an accident` o
    AND ((NOT `the occurrence is treatment`) OR o EQUALS `(f) an internal force during labour causing a Schedule 3A birth injury`)

-- s 26(1)(a)-(e): death, physical injury, the kinds of mental injury, damage
-- to dentures or prostheses. (1A): hearing loss of "5% or more of binaural
-- hearing loss". (2): not "caused wholly or substantially by a gradual
-- process, disease, or infection" unless work-related or treatment (s 20(2)
-- (e)-(h)). (3): not a cardiovascular episode unless s 20(2)(i) or (j).
-- (4): not ageing or natural use of teeth.
@ref s 26
GIVEN i IS AN `Injury facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a personal injury` i IF
        `a kind of harm`
    AND (NOT i's `cause` EQUALS `the ageing process`)
    AND (NOT i's `cause` EQUALS `natural use of teeth or dentures`)
    AND ((NOT i's `cause` EQUALS `a gradual process, disease or infection, not work-related or treatment`) OR i's `consequence of treatment for a covered injury`)
    AND ((NOT i's `cause` EQUALS `a cardiovascular or cerebrovascular episode`) OR i's `a cardiovascular episode from abnormal work effort`)
    WHERE
        `a kind of harm` MEANS
            CONSIDER i's `harm`
            WHEN `hearing loss` pct THEN pct AT LEAST 5
            WHEN `none` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Treatment injury (s 32)`

-- s 32(1): suffered seeking or receiving treatment from a registered health
-- professional, "(b) caused by treatment; and (c) not a necessary part, or
-- ordinary consequence, of the treatment". (2): not "(a) wholly or
-- substantially caused by a person's underlying health condition", "(b)
-- solely attributable to a resource allocation decision", or "(c) a result
-- of a person unreasonably withholding or delaying their consent".
@ref s 32(1)-(3)
GIVEN t IS A `Treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a treatment injury` t IF
        t's `caused by treatment`
    AND (NOT t's `a necessary part or ordinary consequence of the treatment`)
    AND (NOT t's `wholly or substantially caused by an underlying condition`)
    AND (NOT t's `solely a resource allocation decision`)
    AND (NOT t's `unreasonably withheld or delayed consent`)

§§ `Cover (ss 20-24)`

-- s 20(1): cover if suffered "in New Zealand on or after 1 April 2002", a
-- s 26(1)(a), (b), (c) or (e) injury, of a kind in (2): caused by an accident,
-- a treatment injury, a consequence of treatment for covered injury, a
-- work-related gradual process, and the cardiovascular cases. s 23: a person
-- not ordinarily resident has no cover while on (or embarking or
-- disembarking) the ship or aircraft that brings or takes them.
-- s 22(1): outside New Zealand, if "ordinarily resident in New Zealand" and
-- the injury would be covered in New Zealand. s 22(3)-(4): a treatment injury
-- from treatment given outside New Zealand only if suffered "on or after
-- 1 July 2005", and the person "is ordinarily resident in New Zealand when the
-- treatment is given" (FORK F8: for a treatment injury the residence input is
-- read as residence when the treatment was given, and (4)(a)-(b), the
-- provider's equivalent qualifications, are folded into `caused by
-- treatment`).
-- s 21: mental injury from a Schedule 3 act, suffered inside or outside New
-- Zealand, where the act is performed (2)(b) "(i) in New Zealand; or (ii)
-- outside New Zealand on ... a person who is ordinarily resident in New
-- Zealand when the act is performed". s 21B: work-related mental injury from a
-- single sudden event, on or after 1 October 2008, the event occurring
-- (2)(c) in New Zealand or to a person then ordinarily resident. FORK F9: for
-- these two kinds of harm, `in New Zealand` and `ordinarily resident in New
-- Zealand` are read as where the act or event took place and residence at
-- that time; s 21(3), 21B(3) make residence when the injury is suffered
-- irrelevant. Whether the s 21B event qualifies (2)(a)-(b), (5)-(7) is
-- `a qualifying event for work-related mental injury` below.
@ref ss 20-23
GIVEN i IS AN `Injury facts`, `an accident` IS A BOOLEAN, `a treatment injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has cover, injury` i `, accident:` `an accident` `, treatment injury:` `a treatment injury` IF
    CONSIDER i's `harm`
    WHEN `mental injury from a Schedule 3 act (s 21)` THEN
            i's `suffered on` AT LEAST YMD 2002 4 1
        AND `act or event in New Zealand or on a resident`
    WHEN `work-related mental injury from a sudden event (s 21B)` THEN
            i's `suffered on` AT LEAST YMD 2008 10 1
        AND `act or event in New Zealand or on a resident`
    OTHERWISE
            i's `suffered on` AT LEAST YMD 2002 4 1
        AND `a personal injury` i
        AND `of a covered kind`
        AND `where it was suffered`
    WHERE
        `act or event in New Zealand or on a resident` MEANS
            i's `in New Zealand` OR i's `ordinarily resident in New Zealand`
        `of a covered kind` MEANS
               `an accident`
            OR `a treatment injury`
            OR i's `consequence of treatment for a covered injury`
            OR i's `cause` EQUALS `a work-related gradual process, disease or infection`
            OR i's `a cardiovascular episode from abnormal work effort`
        `where it was suffered` MEANS
            IF i's `in New Zealand`
            THEN i's `ordinarily resident in New Zealand` OR (NOT i's `on the ship or aircraft to, around or from New Zealand, or embarking`)
            ELSE     i's `ordinarily resident in New Zealand`
                 AND ((NOT `a treatment injury`) OR i's `suffered on` AT LEAST YMD 2005 7 1)

-- s 17(2)-(3): no permanent place of residence in New Zealand if absent (or
-- intending to be absent) "for more than 6 months"; but one has if present
-- "for a period or periods exceeding in the aggregate 183 days in the
-- 12-month period immediately before last becoming absent". (2) overrides (3).
-- (3) is a sufficient condition, not the only one: a person whose permanent
-- home is New Zealand and who is absent 6 months or less is resident without
-- it.
@ref s 17(1)-(5)
GIVEN `a citizen, resident visa holder, or accompanying family` IS A BOOLEAN, `New Zealand is their permanent home while present` IS A BOOLEAN, `months absent or intended` IS A NUMBER, `days present in the 12 months before leaving` IS A NUMBER, `absent for employment or 6 months after, intending to return` IS A BOOLEAN, `unlawfully in New Zealand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ordinarily resident, qualifying category:` `a citizen, resident visa holder, or accompanying family` `, permanent home while present:` `New Zealand is their permanent home while present` `, months absent` `months absent or intended` `, days present` `days present in the 12 months before leaving` `, absent for work:` `absent for employment or 6 months after, intending to return` `, unlawful:` `unlawfully in New Zealand` IF
        `a citizen, resident visa holder, or accompanying family`
    AND (NOT `unlawfully in New Zealand`)
    AND (   `absent for employment or 6 months after, intending to return`
         OR (    `months absent or intended` AT MOST 6
             AND (   `New Zealand is their permanent home while present`
                  OR `days present in the 12 months before leaving` GREATER THAN 183)))

-- s 21B(2), (5)-(6): the person must experience, see or hear the event
-- "directly" — involved or witnessing it in close physical proximity; not
-- through television, news, radio, telephone or another person; and it must
-- be an event "that could reasonably be expected to cause mental injury to
-- people generally".
@ref s 21B(2), (5)-(7)
GIVEN `involved or witnessed in close proximity` IS A BOOLEAN, `through a secondary source` IS A BOOLEAN, `could injure people generally` IS A BOOLEAN, `a sudden event, not a gradual process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying event for work-related mental injury, direct:` `involved or witnessed in close proximity` `, secondary:` `through a secondary source` `, would injure people generally:` `could injure people generally` `, sudden:` `a sudden event, not a gradual process` IF
    `involved or witnessed in close proximity` AND (NOT `through a secondary source`) AND `could injure people generally` AND `a sudden event, not a gradual process`

-- s 30(2)(c), (2A): a work-related gradual process if employment tasks or
-- environment cause or contribute, and where the property is also present
-- outside work, "it is more likely" the injury came from work; the
-- Corporation may decline if the risk "is not significantly greater" for
-- people doing the task. (3)-(4): a Schedule 2 disease in the listed
-- exposure needs no causation assessment. (4A): exposure in New Zealand, or
-- while ordinarily resident.
@ref s 30(2)-(4A)
GIVEN `a Schedule 2 disease with the listed exposure` IS A BOOLEAN, `work property causes or contributes` IS A BOOLEAN, `more likely from work than non-work` IS A BOOLEAN, `risk significantly greater for those doing the work` IS A BOOLEAN, `exposure in New Zealand or while ordinarily resident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a work-related gradual process injury, Schedule 2:` `a Schedule 2 disease with the listed exposure` `, causes:` `work property causes or contributes` `, more likely work:` `more likely from work than non-work` `, greater risk:` `risk significantly greater for those doing the work` `, local exposure:` `exposure in New Zealand or while ordinarily resident` IF
        `exposure in New Zealand or while ordinarily resident`
    AND (   `a Schedule 2 disease with the listed exposure`
         OR (`work property causes or contributes` AND `more likely from work than non-work` AND `risk significantly greater for those doing the work`))

§§ `Classification and the Account (ss 28, 29, 35, 166-228)`

-- s 35(1): "the movement of a motor vehicle" or a stationary vehicle struck by
-- another conveyance; (2): not loading, unloading, repairing or servicing,
-- use other than as a conveyance, or off-road use (unless off-road because it
-- was out of control, (3)).
@ref s 35
GIVEN v IS A `Vehicle involvement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a motor vehicle injury` v IF
    v EQUALS `the movement of a motor vehicle` OR v EQUALS `a stationary motor vehicle struck by another conveyance`

-- s 35(1)(b): motor vehicle injury "does not include a personal injury that
-- is a work-related mental injury". The vehicle involvement that counts for
-- classification is therefore none for that harm.
@ref s 35(1)(b)
GIVEN h IS A Harm, v IS A `Vehicle involvement`
GIVETH A `Vehicle involvement`
`the vehicle involvement that counts under s 35, harm` h `, vehicle` v MEANS
    IF h EQUALS `work-related mental injury from a sudden event (s 21B)` THEN `no vehicle` ELSE v

-- s 28(1): work-related if suffered at a place for employment, on a meal or
-- rest break at the place of employment, in employer-provided transport, or
-- travelling to treatment for a work injury.
@ref s 28(1)
GIVEN w IS A `Work circumstance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a work-related circumstance` w IF NOT w EQUALS `not at work`

-- s 29: an injury that is both — "(1)" work-related if in s 28(1)(c) or (d)
-- travel; "(2)" a motor vehicle injury if in s 28(1)(a) or (b). s 28(4):
-- work-related gradual process is work-related. s 218(1): non-work means
-- anything else that is not treatment injury. FORK F2: a treatment injury is
-- classified first, because s 228(1) funds it from the Treatment Injury
-- Account except where the treatment was for a work-related injury (s 228(3),
-- s 28(5)).
@ref ss 28, 29, 35, 218(1), 228(3)
GIVEN `treatment injury` IS A BOOLEAN, `treatment for a work injury` IS A BOOLEAN, w IS A `Work circumstance`, v IS A `Vehicle involvement`, `work gradual process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Injury class`
`the class of injury, treatment injury:` `treatment injury` `, for a work injury:` `treatment for a work injury` `, at work:` w `, vehicle:` v `, work gradual process:` `work gradual process` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `treatment injury` AND NOT `treatment for a work injury`         THEN `a treatment injury`
           IF `treatment injury` OR `work gradual process`                      THEN `a work-related personal injury`
           IF `a motor vehicle injury` v AND `a work-related circumstance` w    THEN
               IF w EQUALS `at a place for the purposes of employment` OR w EQUALS `on a meal or rest break at the place of employment`
               THEN `a motor vehicle injury`
               ELSE `a work-related personal injury`
           IF `a motor vehicle injury` v                                        THEN `a motor vehicle injury`
           IF `a work-related circumstance` w                                   THEN `a work-related personal injury`
           OTHERWISE                                                                 `a non-work injury`

-- ss 167, 213, 218, 227, 228: the Work Account funds work-related injury to
-- employees and self-employed; the Motor Vehicle Account motor vehicle
-- injury; the Treatment Injury Account treatment injury; the Earners' Account
-- non-work injury to earners; the Non-Earners' Account non-work injury to
-- non-earners. s 227(3)(b): a foreign representative's employee from the
-- Non-Earners' Account.
@ref ss 167(1), 213(1), 218(2), 227(1), 228(1)
GIVEN c IS AN `Injury class`, s IS AN `Earner status`
GIVETH AN Account
`the Account that pays for` c `, claimant` s MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a treatment injury`             THEN `the Treatment Injury Account`
    WHEN `a work-related personal injury` THEN `the Work Account`
    WHEN `a motor vehicle injury`         THEN `the Motor Vehicle Account`
    WHEN `a non-work injury`              THEN
        IF s EQUALS `a non-earner` OR s EQUALS `a potential earner`
        THEN `the Non-Earners' Account`
        ELSE `the Earners' Account`

§§ `Dates of injury (ss 36-38)`

-- s 37(1): a work-related gradual process injury is suffered on "the earlier"
-- of first treatment by a medical or nurse practitioner for it, and the date
-- it first causes incapacity. (3)-(4): exposure before 1 April 1974 — not
-- earlier than 1 July 1992.
@ref s 37
GIVEN `first treated` IS A MAYBE DATE, `first incapacity` IS A MAYBE DATE, `exposure before 1 April 1974` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`a gradual process injury is suffered on, first treated` `first treated` `, first incapacity` `first incapacity` `, pre-1974 exposure:` `exposure before 1 April 1974` MEANS
    IF `exposure before 1 April 1974` THEN `the later of` (YMD 1992 7 1) `the date` ELSE `the date`
    WHERE
        `the date` MEANS
            CONSIDER `first treated`
            WHEN JUST t THEN
                CONSIDER `first incapacity`
                WHEN JUST i THEN `the earlier of` t i
                WHEN NOTHING THEN t
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                CONSIDER `first incapacity`
                WHEN JUST i THEN i
                WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "s 37(1): neither first treatment nor first incapacity has occurred"

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 1-19, 21A, 24, 25A, 27, 30(5)-(7), 31, 33, 34, 36, 38; Schedules 2, 3, 3A
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`cover provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "ss 1-6, 9-16, 18, 18A: title, commencement, purpose, definitions, earnings, New Zealand, spouse and partner — read into the facts"
         "s 21A: cover deemed under the 1992 Act for mental injury from pre-1992 criminal acts, and its interaction with civil proceedings"
         "s 24: no cover for gradual process from work done outside New Zealand before 1 April 1974 while not resident"
         "s 25A: review of Schedule 3A"
         "s 30(5)-(7): no cover for non-physical stress, or deafness compensated under the 1956 Act"
         "s 33: what treatment includes"
         "s 34: medical misadventure claims before 1 July 2005"
         "ss 36, 38: dates of mental injury (first treatment) and treatment injury (first treatment for the symptoms)"
         "Schedules 2, 3 and 3A: the occupational diseases, the Crimes Act offences and the birth injuries, read as inputs"
